# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# OPEN positive. One callable formal receives a held definition and two
# methods of the unit, each formed in its own way. g0, held in p0 with n
# 100, reads n; g1 reads other, a field of the unit, 9; f0 reads nothing.
# run calls its formal: 105, 10 and 1. under has n 7 and other 20: 12 for
# the held definition, 21 for g1, 1 for f0. This implementation does not
# tell a definition's node from a callable formed in another way where the
# call is made: the call in run is refused where it stands, as a limit and
# no rule. Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: f0 () int
    return: 1
end: f0

fn: g1 () int
    return: other + 1
end: g1

fn: make0 (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: g0 () int
        return: n + 5
    return: g0

@: p0 make0(100)

fn: run (f0: q) int
    return: q()
end: run

fn: under () int
    int: n 7
    int: other 20
    return: run(p0) * 10000 + run(g1) * 100 + run(f0)
end: under

int: a run(p0)
int: b run(g1)
int: c run(f0)
int: d under()
int: ok 7
if: a != 105 || b != 10 || c != 1 || d != 122101
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
